   "why": "The binary's provider selector maps anthropicAws/anthropicGoogleCloud/mantle to these CLAUDE_CODE_USE_* names beside bedrock/vertex/foundry (route-names contexts: `anthropicAws:\"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_ANTHROPIC_AWS\",anthropicGoogleCloud:...,mantle:\"CLAUDE_CODE_USE_MANTLE\",vertex:...`; `Ne(process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_USE_ANTHROPIC_AWS)||...`). CLAUDE_CODE_USE_GATEWAY routes a session through a gateway with ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (\"This session is set up for a ... because CLAUDE_CODE_USE_GATEWAY is set with ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\"); CLAUDE_CODE_PROVIDER_MANAGED_BY_HOST gates it with CLAUDE_CODE_HOST_CREDS_FILE. None matches drive.py's harness patterns (^CLAUDE_CODE_USE_(BEDROCK|VERTEX|FOUNDRY)$) or the generic pattern, so environment_record would not even list them, and none is on the billing-route list, so the money line would not stop on them."
